OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 4 Oct to Tue 13 Oct
OL,6,FHigh pressure will likely be in place
OL,7,Fover southern UK through the first few
OL,8,Fdays of this period. This means plenty
OL,9,Fof dry weather to be had here, albeit
OL,10,Fwith some chilly nights and overnight
OL,11,Fand morning fog in places. In the
OL,12,Fnorth, a rather more changeable
OL,13,Fpattern will continue, with occasional
OL,14,Frain and windy conditions at times.
OL,15,FBroadly changeable weather patterns
OL,16,Flook to continue through to mid-month,
OL,17,Fwith ridges of high pressure extending
OL,18,Ffrom the southwest, interspersed by
OL,19,FAtlantic frontal systems. These could
OL,20,Fbe associated with quite deep and fast-
OL,21,Fmoving depressions, bringing the
OL,22,Fpotential for windy weather more
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fwidely, but perhaps more likely in the
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fnorth and east. Temperatures probably
OL,25,Fnear or slightly above normal overall,
OL,26,Fbut with some day to day oscillations.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
